course: dictionary
lesson: 6721
title: Offshore
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Offshore is built from two parts: off and shore. The shore is the land at the edge of the sea, so offshore means away from the shore, out in the sea. Try this in a sentence: «Offshore wind farms are rows of turbines standing in the sea, where the wind is stronger and steadier.» Turbines standing in the sea fits the meaning perfectly, so offshore must mean in the sea, away from the coast.
explain: The context also shows you how the word works. «The cables carry the electricity to land» tells you the wind farm is out at sea and the power comes back to the shore. An offshore wind is different: it blows from the land out towards the sea. You can check this by swapping your meaning into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
explain: Offshore can also appear in money news. «Offshore accounts» are kept in another country, often to pay less tax, so the sea is not the meaning there. When a word has more than one meaning, read the words around it to find the right one.
fact: Offshore means in the sea, away from the coast.
fact: An offshore wind blows from the land out towards the sea.
fact: An offshore wind farm is a group of turbines standing in the sea.
fact: An offshore island lies off the coast.
fact: On a windy beach, an offshore wind can blow inflatables and swimmers out to sea, so always be careful.
exercise: «Offshore wind farms are rows of turbines standing in the sea.» Where are the turbines standing? | On the land, near the houses | Underground, under the roads | *In the sea, away from the coast | Inside a big city
exercise: What is an offshore wind? | A wind that only blows at night | An onshore wind that blows into the land | A wind that never moves | *A wind that blows from the land out towards the sea
exercise: If an offshore wind blows on a beach, what might happen to an inflatable? | *It can be blown out to sea | It turns into a boat | It floats back to the shore | It sinks into the sand
test: «The biggest offshore turbines have blades more than 100 metres long.» Where do these turbines stand? | *In the sea, away from the coast | Children playing in the park | Shops on the high street | Trees in a forest
test: What is an offshore island? | A dry island in the desert | *An island lying off the coast | An island in a lake | An island in the middle of a city
exam: In the money sense, what do offshore accounts often do? | *Are kept in another country, often to pay less tax | Float on the sea | Blow towards the shore | Make a cake for the school fair
